I am pleased to announce the release of GNU Ocrad 0.12.

Ocrad is the GNU OCR (Optical Character Recognition) program.

The homepage is at http://www.gnu.org/software/ocrad/ocrad.html.

The sources can be dowloaded from http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/ocrad/ or from
your favorite GNU mirror.

The md5sum is:
72ee02108c3fa33ee60525ca01976940  ocrad-0.12.tar.bz2

This release is also GPG signed. You can download the signature by
appending ".sig" to the URL.

Changes in version 0.12:

* Change in internal representation; The blockmap has been eliminated.

* The text inside tables of solid lines is now recognized.

* Improvements in character recognition have been made.

* A possible integer overflow when loading pbm file has been fixed.

* The GPL has been updated to version 2.3.


Please send bug reports and suggestions to <bug-ocrad@gnu.org>.


Regards,
Antonio Diaz, GNU Ocrad author and maintainer.



