The iptables ROPE module (from the P2PWall project) enables users to 
write IP packet matching logic using a simple and safe scripting 
language. Scripts are installed into iptables chains using the iptables 
command and have "read-only" access to all the packet header fields and 
the data payload.

Example scripts are povided to identify Gnutella, Bittorrent, eDonkey 
2000 and large HTTP downloads. Work on a range other popular P2P 
protocols is in progress.

The 20050613 release supplies the following changes..

1. The "ne" keyword has been fixed. Previous versions reversed the sense
    of the test.

For documentation, tutorial, dowloads and sample scripts, vist the ROPE 
project home page at: http://www.lowth.com/rope.

